WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.544
Full autonomy does not mean doing every possible procedure. It means taking responsibility for noticing the whole situation, stating the priority, selecting an authorized next step and checking the result without waiting for prompts.
完全自主并不意味着执行所有可能的操作，而是主动识别整体情境、说清优先事项、选择获准的下一步并核验结果，不等待提示。

00:00:14.544 --> 00:00:32.760
Before acting, name the patient’s immediate needs, the device concern, what is unknown and which resource or provider can help. A nurse’s or advanced practitioner’s device procedure does not transfer to a PCP just because it appears in a textbook or training scenario.
行动前应说明患者即时需求、器械问题、未知信息及可求助的资源或执业者。护理人员或高级执业者的器械操作不会因为出现在教材或情景训练中就转移给 PCP。

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:53.136
The Week 13 school objective says not to remove or reposition a device unless there is an immediate life threat. Apply that instruction to this learning scenario. It is not a blanket clinical rule for every device; current device-specific guidance, provider scope and service direction govern actual practice.
第13周学校目标要求：除非存在立即生命威胁，否则不要拔除或重置器械。本情景按此教学目标练习。这不是适用于所有器械的普遍临床规则；实际处置须遵循器械专属现行指导、执业权限和服务指示。

00:00:53.136 --> 00:01:10.992
If an immediate threat develops, act only within a current pathway, your licence and applicable rescue training. This lecture does not teach tube insertion, catheter flushing, replacement or adjustment. Use direct instructor supervision for any hands-on device lab.
若出现立即威胁，只能依照现行流程、个人执照及适用急救训练行动。本课不教授置管、冲洗导尿管、更换或调整器械。任何器械实操都应由教官直接监督。

00:01:10.992 --> 00:01:28.656
A 55-year-old woman at home has new abdominal pain and nausea. A family member reports that her feeding tube shifted while she was being moved. The patient looks uncomfortable, and there is moisture near the dressing; no one can confirm when the tube was last used.
一名55岁女性在家出现新的腹痛和恶心。家属说患者移动时喂养管发生移位。患者显得不适，敷料附近有潮湿，但无人能确认上次使用该管的时间。

00:01:28.656 --> 00:01:53.952
This original case follows the school objective without reproducing a web case stem. Do not use, remove or reposition the displaced tube. Assess airway, breathing, circulation, pain, abdominal appearance and any systemic change; obtain the device name, baseline and last-use history, then follow current guidance and arrange appropriate escalation.
本原创案例遵循学校目标，但不复述网站题干。不要使用、拔除或重置移位的管路。评估气道、呼吸、循环、疼痛、腹部外观及全身变化；询问器械名称、基线和最后使用时间，再遵循现行指导并安排适当升级处置。

00:01:53.952 --> 00:02:12.888
Report the actual device label or the caregiver’s description, where it enters or exits, the visible external length if marked, and what has changed. Observe the site without advancing, rotating, flushing or testing patency. Do not infer internal placement from appearance.
报告设备标签或照护者描述、进出位置、若有外部标记则记录可见长度，以及发生了什么变化。观察器械周围，但不要推进、旋转、冲洗或测试通畅度。不能根据外观推断内部位置正确。

00:02:12.888 --> 00:02:32.856
Abdominal pain plus leakage, increasing tenderness, fever, vomiting, distension or deteriorating perfusion raises concern and requires prompt assessment. These findings do not prove peritonitis or sepsis; use the current abdominal-pain or sepsis pathway and communicate the uncertainty.
腹痛合并渗漏、压痛加剧、发热、呕吐、腹胀或灌注恶化会提高警惕，需要及时评估。但这些发现不能单独证明腹膜炎或脓毒症；应使用现行腹痛或脓毒症流程，并说明不确定性。

00:02:32.856 --> 00:02:52.224
A long-term-care resident has become newly confused and weak. Staff report that little urine has entered the drainage bag over several hours; the urine looks darker than usual, and they believe the catheter may be blocked. The patient is warm, breathing faster than usual and less interactive.
一名长期护理院居民新近出现意识混乱和虚弱。工作人员报告过去几小时尿袋中尿量很少，尿液比平时颜色深，并认为导尿管可能堵塞。患者身体发热、呼吸比平时快、互动减少。

00:02:52.224 --> 00:03:14.880
The device may be part of the story, but the patient’s systemic change is the priority. Obtain the time course, baseline cognition, observed output and device history; assess perfusion and other sepsis cues, follow the current sepsis pathway and request appropriate support. Do not manipulate the catheter without current authorization and direction.
器械问题可能是情境的一部分，但患者全身变化才是重点。询问时间线、认知基线、观察到的尿量及器械史；评估灌注和其他脓毒症线索，遵循现行脓毒症流程并请求适当支援。没有现行授权和指示时，不要操作导尿管。

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:30.816
Low volume in the collection bag describes drainage, not a confirmed measure of kidney urine production. Consider the time interval, baseline, possible leakage or obstruction and other illness; do not infer one cause from the bag alone.
尿袋中的尿量描述的是引流量，并非肾脏尿液生成量的确证测量。应考虑时间段、基线、可能渗漏或堵塞及其他疾病；不能仅凭尿袋确定病因。

00:03:30.816 --> 00:03:44.016
Urine colour, smell or appearance alone is not a diagnosis of urinary infection or sepsis. Assess the whole patient and escalate through the current pathway rather than manipulating the device.
单凭尿液颜色、气味或外观不能诊断尿路感染或脓毒症。应评估患者整体状况并依现行流程升级处置，而非操作器械。

00:03:44.016 --> 00:03:59.736
Look for a change from baseline and combine respiratory effort, perfusion, mental status, measured observations and the patient’s story. If the patient is deteriorating, communicate that urgency before discussing device troubleshooting.
应寻找相对基线的变化，并结合呼吸功、灌注、意识、客观测量和患者叙述。若患者正在恶化，应先明确传达紧急程度，再讨论器械排障。

00:03:59.736 --> 00:04:15.912
A useful handover describes the device in neutral terms: name or type if known, when it last functioned normally, what output was seen and what the caregiver observed. Attribute information to its source and distinguish measured output from estimates.
有效交接应客观描述器械：已知的名称或类型、最近一次正常工作的时间、观察到的输出，以及照护者的报告。注明信息来源，并区分实测输出与估计值。

00:04:15.912 --> 00:04:31.800
Also report the patient’s baseline and change, site findings, relevant medicines or recent feeding, consultation, and the reason the device was left in place. A device status is part of the handover, not a replacement for a full patient assessment.
还应报告患者基线与变化、入口处发现、相关药物或近期喂养、咨询意见及器械保持原位的原因。器械状态只是交接的一部分，不能替代完整患者评估。

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:46.344
The school weekend asks learners to manage two patients simultaneously. State which person has the most time-critical threat and why, assign a named partner to the other patient, and tell both teams when to report a change.
学校周末要求学习者同时处理两名患者。应说明哪位患者的威胁最具时间敏感性及原因，指定队友负责另一名患者，并告诉双方何时报告变化。

00:04:46.344 --> 00:05:01.560
A plan is not autonomous if the second patient disappears from attention. Use a timer or spoken check-back, delegate repeat observations within training and request another crew or clinical support when available capacity is insufficient.
如果第二名患者从关注中消失，计划就不算自主。应使用计时器或口头复核，在训练范围内分派重复观察；可用人手不足时，应请求另一组人员或临床支援。

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:30.624
Return to the patient with the displaced feeding tube. The patient is worried about missing nutrition, while a family member wants the crew to put the tube back immediately. First hear the patient's own concern and assess the current symptoms. The school's patient-centered-care reading treats the patient as a team member with physical, emotional and social needs, not as the object of a device repair. Respect the concern without promising an unsafe or unauthorized intervention.
回到喂养管移位的患者。患者担心无法获得营养，家属则希望急救人员立即把管子放回。应先听取患者本人的担忧，评估当前症状。指定阅读把患者视为有生理、情绪和社会需要的团队成员，而非等待维修器械的对象。尊重其担忧，不等于承诺不安全或未经授权的操作。

00:05:30.624 --> 00:06:04.056
Explain what you observed, what remains uncertain and what safe assessment, support or consultation you can offer. Invite the patient's preferences and ask them to explain the agreed next step in their own words. A nod or a relative's answer does not establish understanding. Language, hearing, vision or literacy barriers call for suitable support; they are not automatic evidence of incapacity. Patient-centered communication is a clinical action, not a promise that every requested treatment will be provided.
解释观察到的情况、仍不确定的事项，以及可以提供的安全评估、支持或咨询。邀请患者表达偏好，并请患者用自己的话说明已同意的下一步。点头或家属代答，不能证明患者已经理解。语言、听力、视力或读写困难需要适当支持，并不自动意味着缺乏决定能力。以患者为中心，也不意味着必须提供每一项被要求的治疗。

00:06:04.056 --> 00:06:35.616
In our original variation, the patient accepts examination but says they do not want the tube handled and are unsure about transport. Clarify each decision rather than documenting refuses everything. Use the applicable consent and refusal framework, explain the risks and reasonable alternatives, assess the relevant ability and seek required consultation. A family majority, a psychiatric history or the fact that the choice worries you does not by itself remove the patient's authority.
在这个原创分支中，患者同意接受检查，但不愿别人触碰管路，也尚未决定是否转运。应逐项澄清，不能记录成拒绝一切照护。依适用的同意与拒绝框架，解释风险及合理替代方案，评估与具体决定相关的能力，并取得必要咨询。家属的多数意见、精神病史或令人担忧的选择，本身都不会取消患者的决定权。

00:06:35.616 --> 00:07:04.800
Continue care that is accepted and authorized while resolving uncertainty. The reading's potential benefits include trust, error prevention, self-management and a more feasible plan; they are not guarantees of compliance or recovery. Check whether the patient can obtain the agreed help and what support is actually available. A plan that looks correct on a form can still fail if no one understands it or the next service has not accepted responsibility.
澄清未知事项时，应继续提供患者接受且属于授权范围内的照护。阅读提出的潜在效益包括建立信任、预防错误、支持自我管理和形成可实施的计划，但并不保证依从或康复。要确认患者能否实际获得已同意的帮助。纸面方案即使正确，若无人理解或下一个服务尚未接受责任，仍可能失败。

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:36.672
While you discuss the feeding-tube problem, the second patient's catheter pain increases. Assign an appropriate colleague to assess that person and report actual findings, not just to watch them. Retain an overview of both patients and change priority if systemic deterioration appears. The nursing text's delegation carryover emphasizes supervision and evaluation, but the actual PCP licence, competence and service policy determine what may be assigned. Giving a task does not erase the need for feedback.
讨论喂养管问题时，另一名患者的导尿管相关疼痛加重。应安排有能力且获授权的同事评估，并回报实际发现，而不只是请人看着。保持两名患者的整体情况可见，全身状况恶化时重新排序。护理阅读强调任务分派后的监督与评价；实际能分派什么，仍由PCP执照、个人能力和机构政策决定。分派任务不能省略反馈。

00:07:36.672 --> 00:08:08.928
The collaborative-care reading identifies organized communication, effective protected data sharing, simplified referrals and coordinated scheduling. Together they reduce gaps between people and services. Ask for the expertise the problem needs, communicate urgency and confirm a feasible next step. A referral message sent is not an accepted appointment, and a portal upload is not an accepted clinical handover. State who is coordinating the plan and who will act if the patient changes.
协作阅读提出有组织的沟通、有效且受保护的数据分享、简化转介和协调安排，以减少人员与服务之间的缺口。请求与问题相匹配的专长，说明紧急程度，并核实下一步确实可行。发送转介消息不等于预约已被接受，上传门户也不等于临床交接完成。要明确谁协调计划，以及患者变化时由谁行动。

00:08:08.928 --> 00:08:42.384
At handover, give the device type and observed status, symptoms and trends, actions and response, the patient's actual decisions and remaining uncertainty. Confirm the receiving capability and explicit acceptance. Use the secure authorized record route, but do not mistake copying a medication list for reconciling it or assume every team member needs the entire record. Transparent communication includes correcting uncertainty and inaccuracy rather than disguising them with confident wording.
交接应包括器械类型、观察到的状态、症状趋势、行动及反应、患者的实际决定和剩余未知。核实接收方的能力及其明确接受。使用安全、获准的记录渠道；复制用药表不等于完成药物核对，也不能假设每位队员都需要全部资料。透明沟通包括正视未知和错误，而非用自信措辞掩盖。

00:08:42.384 --> 00:09:13.296
During debrief, compare the intended plan with what both patients and the team actually understood and did. Did communication uncover a safety issue? Was the agreed service accessible? Did the second patient receive a real assessment? Could the receiving clinician follow the reasoning? Potential convenience and resource savings should be evaluated, not promised. The school's timed PCR target does not justify omitting an unresolved clinical concern or an unaccepted transition.
复盘时，比较原定计划与两名患者及团队实际理解、执行的内容。沟通是否发现安全问题？患者能否获得已同意的服务？第二名患者是否真正接受了评估？接收人员能否看懂推理？便利和节省资源只是需要评价的潜在效益，并非保证。学校的PCR限时不能成为漏记临床担忧或未完成责任移交的理由。

00:09:13.296 --> 00:09:33.480
Before any medication action, verify the patient, medication identity, strength, indication, route, calculated amount, timing, allergy status and expiry using the current service monograph and policy. Visually inspect the product and use the required label if it is removed from its package.
采取任何给药行动前，应按现行服务药物专论和政策核对患者、药物名称、浓度、适应证、途径、计算量、时间、过敏状态及有效期。目视检查药品；若药物离开原包装，应按要求清晰标注。

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:51.360
A mnemonic is not a substitute for an authorized indication, a correct calculation, consultation or documented administration. If the drug, patient, dose or route is uncertain, pause and resolve the uncertainty with the approved resource instead of guessing.
记忆口诀不能替代获准的适应证、正确计算、咨询或给药记录。若药物、患者、剂量或途径不确定，应暂停并使用批准的资源澄清，不要猜测。

00:09:51.360 --> 00:10:07.920
Medication errors and near misses are safety signals. Follow the service reporting process, document the patient response and notify the appropriate clinical lead. This lesson does not replace medication-math gating or hands-on competency assessment.
用药错误和险些发生的错误都是安全信号。应遵循服务报告流程，记录患者反应并通知相应临床负责人。本课不能替代药物计算闸门考核或实际操作能力评估。

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:26.376
Nausea may accompany serious conditions, including acute coronary syndrome, stroke, sepsis, glucose disturbance, gastrointestinal bleeding, toxic exposure or pregnancy. Assess the patient and likely cause rather than treating nausea as a stand-alone problem.
恶心可能伴随急性冠脉综合征、中风、脓毒症、血糖异常、消化道出血、中毒暴露或妊娠等严重情况。应评估患者和可能病因，而不是把恶心当作孤立问题。

00:10:26.376 --> 00:10:48.456
BCEHS E07 lists provider-level antiemetic options, including PCP options. Before administration, follow current monographs, training, indication, contraindications, dose and route. The school reading on antiemetics does not authorize any drug outside the learner’s current licence and service direction.
BCEHS E07 列出不同执业层级的止吐选择，包括 PCP 选项。给药前应遵循现行药物专论、培训要求、适应证、禁忌证、剂量和途径。学校止吐药阅读不能授权学习者超出当前执照和服务指示用药。

00:10:48.456 --> 00:11:02.856
After symptom treatment, reassess nausea, hydration, airway risk, mental status and the underlying concern. Improvement in one symptom does not prove the dangerous cause has been excluded.
症状治疗后，应复评恶心、脱水、气道风险、意识及潜在问题。单一症状改善不能证明危险病因已经排除。

00:11:02.856 --> 00:11:19.896
Valve stenosis limits forward flow through an opening; regurgitation allows blood to move backward through an incompletely closed valve. Either can alter cardiac workload and may contribute to reduced exercise tolerance, dyspnea, fatigue or syncope.
瓣膜狭窄会限制血液通过瓣口的前向流动；瓣膜返流则因关闭不全而使血液反向流动。两者都可能改变心脏负荷，并与活动耐量下降、气短、疲惫或晕厥有关。

00:11:19.896 --> 00:11:36.984
A murmur is a sound produced by turbulent flow, not a measurement of how severe the disease is or what is causing today’s symptoms. Ask about known history and change from baseline; assess current perfusion and follow the applicable cardiac pathway.
杂音是血流湍流产生的声音，不是疾病严重程度的测量，也不能单独说明今天症状的病因。应询问已知病史和基线变化，评估当前灌注并遵循适用的心脏流程。

00:11:36.984 --> 00:11:56.784
The sympathetic nervous system supports rapid responses such as increased heart rate and vascular tone; parasympathetic influence supports restorative functions. Pain, fear, hypoxia or shock may activate a stress response, but tachycardia alone does not identify which cause is present.
交感神经系统支持心率和血管张力等快速反应；副交感影响则参与恢复性功能。疼痛、恐惧、缺氧或休克都可能触发应激反应，但单独心动过速无法确定具体原因。

00:11:56.784 --> 00:12:15.072
Fluid balance affects circulation and may be influenced by intake, losses, renal function and medication. Acid-base balance is linked to carbon dioxide managed by ventilation and bicarbonate regulated by the kidneys; respiratory and metabolic disturbances can interact.
体液平衡影响循环，并受到摄入、丢失、肾功能和药物影响。酸碱平衡与通气调节的二氧化碳及肾脏调节的碳酸氢盐有关；呼吸性和代谢性紊乱可能相互作用。

00:12:15.072 --> 00:12:29.184
Use these mechanisms to ask better questions about vomiting, fluid intake, medications and baseline disease. They do not allow a prehospital learner to infer an arterial blood gas or prescribe fluid from a vague symptom.
这些机制可帮助提出更好的问题，例如呕吐、液体摄入、用药和基线疾病；但不能让院前学习者凭模糊症状推断动脉血气或开具液体治疗。

00:12:29.184 --> 00:13:02.952
Return to the two device patients. Pain, fear, medicines and illness can all change autonomic activity. Follow the circuit: sympathetic outflow is thoracolumbar; parasympathetic outflow is craniosacral. Both use acetylcholine at the ganglion, while the transmitter and receptor at the organ determine the effect. The adrenal medulla adds a circulating catecholamine signal. A large pupil or fast pulse is a finding to interpret, not a specific drug or disease diagnosis.
回到两名有器械问题的患者。疼痛、恐惧、药物和疾病都可能改变自主神经活动。沿通路理解：交感神经为胸腰段流出，副交感神经为脑骶段流出；两者在神经节均使用乙酰胆碱，靶器官的递质与受体则决定具体效应。肾上腺髓质还向循环释放儿茶酚胺。瞳孔扩大或心率加快是需要解释的发现，不是某种药物或疾病的诊断。

00:13:02.952 --> 00:13:37.296
Connect the mechanism to the complaint. Alpha, beta and muscarinic effects differ between vessels, heart, airway, glands and smooth muscle. A medicine can therefore improve one intended symptom while affecting circulation, alertness or bladder function. Check the actual product, timing and patient response. For a patient who becomes dizzy with movement, compare volume, posture, pulse and perfusion rather than explaining everything as anxiety or assuming the autonomic reflex worked normally.
把机制与主诉联系起来。α、β及毒蕈碱受体在血管、心脏、气道、腺体和平滑肌的作用不同，因此药物可能改善目标症状，同时影响循环、清醒程度或膀胱功能。核对实际产品、使用时间及反应。移动后头晕时，应结合容量状态、体位、脉搏及灌注，不能全部归因于焦虑，也不能假定自主反射正常。

00:13:37.296 --> 00:14:12.288
Most body water is within cells; extracellular water includes interstitial fluid and plasma. Sodium and potassium have different relative distributions, and cell membranes determine movement. Edema in one compartment does not prove adequate circulating volume. Thirst, antidiuretic hormone, renal handling and renin-angiotensin-aldosterone signaling regulate water and electrolytes over different timescales. These mechanisms help explain the findings but do not supply an unmeasured electrolyte result.
人体大部分水分位于细胞内，细胞外液则包括组织间液与血浆。钠、钾的相对分布不同，细胞膜影响物质移动。某个区室水肿，并不证明有效循环容量充足。口渴、抗利尿激素、肾脏处理及肾素—血管紧张素—醛固酮信号，在不同时间尺度调节水和电解质。这些机制有助解释发现，却不能提供尚未测量的电解质结果。

00:14:12.288 --> 00:14:45.864
In the feeding-tube case, ask about actual intake, vomiting and other losses. In the catheter case, low collected urine may reflect reduced production, obstruction, displacement or a collection problem. Examine the patient and observed device status before attributing the number to kidney failure. A fluid calculation or a normal pressure does not prove that a bolus is indicated. Follow the current authorized pathway and evaluate the response, including any sign that breathing or perfusion worsens.
喂养管案例要询问实际摄入、呕吐及其他丢失。导尿管收集量少，可能来自尿液生成减少、梗阻、移位或收集问题。诊断肾衰竭之前，应评估患者并检查可见器械状况。补液算术正确或血压正常，都不能证明有补液指征；应遵循现行授权流程，评价反应，包括呼吸或灌注恶化的迹象。

00:14:45.864 --> 00:15:21.624
The bicarbonate and carbon dioxide relationship links lung and kidney function. Reduced alveolar ventilation can raise carbon dioxide and favor respiratory acidosis; increased elimination can favor respiratory alkalosis. Added metabolic acid or bicarbonate loss can cause metabolic acidosis, while gastric acid loss may favor metabolic alkalosis. Compensation moves pH toward baseline but does not establish cure, and two primary problems can coexist. Rate alone does not measure effective ventilation.
碳酸氢盐与二氧化碳的关系把肺和肾联系起来。肺泡通气不足可使二氧化碳升高，促成呼吸性酸中毒；排出增加可促成呼吸性碱中毒。代谢性酸增加或碳酸氢盐丢失可致代谢性酸中毒，胃酸丢失可促成代谢性碱中毒。代偿使pH趋向基线，不等于治愈；两种原发紊乱可同时存在，呼吸频率本身也不能测定有效通气。

00:15:21.624 --> 00:15:55.968
A vomiting patient with deep breathing needs an assessment, not an automatic acid-base label. Compare illness, intake, glucose as indicated, renal history, medicines, possible exposures and the respiratory and perfusion trends. When interpreting a blood-gas result, preserve arterial or venous sample identity, time and treatment context; a normal pH can conceal competing processes. Explain what would increase urgency and request the appropriate resources while immediate support continues.
患者既呕吐又深呼吸时，需要评估，不能自动贴上酸碱诊断。结合疾病、摄入、必要的血糖测量、肾病史、药物暴露及呼吸和灌注趋势。解读血气时要保留动脉或静脉样本、采样时间及治疗背景；正常pH可能掩盖相互抵消的过程。继续即时支持，同时说明哪些变化提高紧急程度，并请求适当资源。

00:15:55.968 --> 00:16:33.504
The CPSC reading has two tracks: the literal assigned pages concern drains, while the named Chapter six framework concerns medicine safety. For our nauseated patient, begin with the current indication and patient assessment. Check allergies by reaction, relevant medicines, product and formulation, dose units, route, contraindications and the required monitoring. Prepare for one patient at a time and protect the preparation from avoidable interruption. An unknown syringe or an unclear instruction must be resolved before use.
CPSC指定阅读有两条线索：字面页码对应引流管，而点名的第六章框架讨论用药安全。对恶心患者，先核实现行指征并完成相关评估，再查过敏反应、相关药物、产品与剂型、剂量单位、途径、禁忌及监测要求。一次只为一名患者备药，减少可避免的打断。来源不明的针筒或含糊指示，必须在使用前澄清。

00:16:33.504 --> 00:17:08.088
Use the actual rights and label checks, not a recital that skips evidence. The textbook lists seven rights; the school may expand the framework. Recheck at retrieval, preparation and before administration, label prepared medicine as required and use a genuinely independent check where required. A tube problem is not permission to give a drug through that tube. Explain the treatment, respect the patient's choice, observe delivery and response, then document what actually happened rather than pre-signing a planned dose.
实际完成用药正确性与标签核查，不能只背口诀而跳过证据。教材列出七项正确核对，学校可能采用扩展框架。取药时、备药时及给药前都要复核，按要求标注已配制药物，并在需要时完成真正独立的核查。管路有问题不代表可以经该管给药。解释治疗、尊重选择、观察实际给药及反应，再记录真实发生的内容，不能预先签署计划剂量。

00:17:08.088 --> 00:17:40.008
High-alert classification concerns the seriousness of harm if a medicine is used in error. It does not mean every such medicine produces errors more often. Use layered safeguards and the actual service requirements; a second person merely agreeing with your calculation is not an independent check. Several patients, repeated doses, distraction and fatigue also create risk. A patient asking why a medicine looks different can reveal a real error, so pause and investigate.
高警示药物的分类关注用错时可能造成的严重伤害，不表示每种这类药物都更容易出错。采取多层防护，遵守实际机构要求；第二人仅仅同意计算结果，不算独立核查。多患者、重复给药、打断和疲劳也会增加风险。患者询问药物为何不同，可能揭示真实错误，应暂停并核查。

00:17:40.008 --> 00:18:15.696
The source's scheduled-dose timing table belongs to an older acute-care policy context, not a new rule for delaying emergency care. Check the actual indication, previous dose and local requirement rather than inventing a due time. Electronic orders, barcodes and controlled dispensing can reduce some errors but can also transmit wrong data. Reconcile the medicine history, check the patient and record actual administration. If something goes wrong, assess and protect the patient first, then communicate and report through the appropriate system.
来源中的定时给药窗口属于既有急性护理政策背景，不是允许延迟急救的新规则。核实真实指征、既往剂量及本地要求，不能编造到期时间。电子医嘱、条码和受控发药可减少部分错误，也可能传播错误资料。仍须核对药史、患者本人及实际给药。出错后先保护患者，再依适用体系沟通和报告。

00:18:15.696 --> 00:18:50.256
The literal CPSC pages show compressed-reservoir Hemovac and JP systems and a curled pigtail example. The photographs explain how a particular system works, not a universal instruction to open, flush, replace or remove every device. Identify the actual device, intended destination and management plan. Shape alone does not establish the suction arrangement. Support the patient and preserve the observed system without improvising an invasive repair outside your training and authority.
CPSC字面指定页展示Hemovac、JP压缩储液器及卷曲的pigtail引流管。照片说明特定系统的工作方式，不是打开、冲洗、更换或拔除所有器械的通用指令。识别实际器械、预定引流位置和管理方案；仅凭形状不能确定负压设置。支持患者，维持观察到的系统状态，不能临时实施超出训练或权限的侵入性维修。

00:18:50.256 --> 00:19:23.112
A fall in output could reflect less production, obstruction, displacement or lost suction. Compare symptoms, perfusion, the insertion site and the visible tubing, and identify multiple drains separately in handover. The source's routine emptying fractions and shift interval are planned nursing examples, not reasons to wait when the patient worsens. Removal requires the actual plan and appropriate clinician; its Hemovac or JP introduction does not supply a pigtail-removal procedure.
引流量下降可能来自液体生成减少、堵塞、移位或负压丧失。结合患者症状、灌注、入口及可见管路判断；多条管路应分别交接。来源中的常规排空比例和班次只是计划护理示例，不意味着患者恶化时可以等待。移除需要真实医嘱及适当人员；Hemovac或JP移除章节的开头，也不提供pigtail的移除步骤。

00:19:23.112 --> 00:19:51.936
Autonomy means owning the whole plan, not working alone. Use the cumulative reader to connect the actual presentation with the relevant pathway and provider row, consultation and reassessment. The crew is one microsystem linked to other teams, supplies, policies and resources. A missing service or connector needs an accepted alternative and a system report, not an invented destination or a borrowed medicine from another patient.
自主意味着对整体计划负责，而不是独自完成所有行动。利用累计阅读，把实际表现与适用流程、执业层级、咨询和复评联系起来。机组是连接其他团队、物资、政策及资源的微系统。服务衔接缺失时，需要已被接受的替代计划及系统报告，不能虚构目的地或借用另一名患者的药物。

00:19:51.936 --> 00:20:25.488
Understand system frameworks accurately. IHI's Triple Aim concerns care experience, population health and per-person cost; its expanded framework separately recognizes workforce well-being and equity. Saving money does not automatically create equitable access. In this case, ask whether the actual patient can understand and reach the agreed next service, who accepted responsibility and what happens if the first plan fails. A portal upload or a referral sent is not the same as that closed loop.
准确理解系统框架。IHI的Triple Aim关注照护体验、人群健康和人均成本，扩展框架另纳入从业者福祉与公平。节省费用不会自动创造公平或可及性。本案要问：患者能否理解并到达已同意的服务？谁接受后续责任？首选计划失败怎么办？上传门户或发送转介，不等于完成闭环。

00:20:25.488 --> 00:20:56.616
The assigned VSM page is a chapter summary, not a new threshold chart. It asks you to interpret pressure as an objective cue alongside baseline, earlier values, pulse and subjective and objective findings. Check measurement quality and context before treating an isolated number as a conclusion. Pain, posture, movement, medicines and illness can all affect a reading. A normal pressure does not exclude an important perfusion, abdominal or device problem.
VSM指定页是章节小结，不是新的阈值表。它要求把血压作为客观线索，结合基线、既往数值、脉搏以及主观和客观发现。把孤立数字作为结论前，要核对测量质量与背景；疼痛、体位、移动、药物和疾病均可影响血压。正常血压不能排除重要的灌注、腹部或器械问题。

00:20:56.616 --> 00:21:29.088
Repeat and trend observations while care continues, and recheck sooner when the condition changes. Do not interpret the book's repeat-measurement advice as a demand to delay support until a second pressure is obtained. For each of the two patients, state the main threat, actual trend, authorized action, expected response and escalation trigger. Record the decisions and an accepted next plan. That integrates physiology, safe implementation and systems-based autonomy.
照护中应持续追踪，病情变化时提前复评。不能把教材的复测建议解释为必须等第二次血压后才提供支持。对两名患者都要说清主要威胁、真实趋势、授权行动、预期反应和升级触发点，并记录决定及已被接受的后续计划。这样才能把生理、安全实施与系统层面的自主照护整合起来。

00:21:29.088 --> 00:21:43.968
Blood pressure is one measurement of pressure in the arterial system. Its significance depends on the patient, baseline, symptoms, technique and the other circulation findings. A single reading cannot establish adequate perfusion.
血压是动脉系统压力的一项测量。其意义取决于患者、基线、症状、测量方法及其他循环表现。单次读数无法确定灌注充分。

00:21:43.968 --> 00:22:01.272
Check cuff size and placement, patient position and measurement conditions. Compare repeated values with mental status, skin, pulse quality and clinical response. A stable pressure does not cancel new confusion, cool skin or a weaker pulse.
核对袖带尺寸与位置、患者体位及测量条件。把重复读数与意识、皮肤、脉搏质量及临床反应比较。血压稳定不能抵消新发意识混乱、皮肤发凉或脉搏减弱。

00:22:01.272 --> 00:22:14.712
A care plan becomes clinically useful when the team implements a specific authorized action and then checks whether the expected change occurred. State the measure or observation that will show success before acting.
照护计划只有在团队实施一项具体获准行动并检查预期变化是否出现后，才真正有临床价值。行动前应先说明用什么测量或观察判断成功。

00:22:14.712 --> 00:22:29.280
If the patient is unchanged or worse, do not keep repeating the same action because it was in the plan. Reconsider the hypothesis, equipment, timing and available pathway; request support and document the new reasoning.
若患者没有变化或更差，不要因为某项行动写在计划里就反复执行。应重新考虑假设、设备、时间及可用流程，寻求支援并记录新的推理。

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:55.944
Return to our feeding-tube and catheter patients. You have a plan, but now distinguish a request from delivery. Did the other patient actually receive an assessment? Did the intended support reach the first patient? Implementation needs an appropriate, accepted and authorized action, the right person and working resources. A task on the board or a treatment prepared in advance is not proof of care delivered.
回到喂养管和导尿管患者。制定计划后，还要区分提出请求与真正落实。另一名患者是否实际接受了评估？预定支持是否送达第一名患者？实施需要合适、被接受且获授权的行动，以及适当人员和可用资源。任务写在板上，或提前备好治疗用品，都不能证明照护已经发生。

00:22:55.944 --> 00:23:23.976
FON Chapter fourteen links implementation, evaluation and documentation. Use one repeated loop: state the expected response, act, observe what changed and revise when the result is inadequate or harmful. Evaluation is not reserved for the end of the call or a later long-term review. Immediate patient needs, preferences and evidence can change the plan before a routine task is finished.
FON第十四章把实施、评价和记录连接起来。反复执行同一循环：说明预期、采取行动、观察变化，结果不足或出现伤害时修订。评价不只发生在呼叫结束或远期复核时。患者的即时需要、偏好及新证据，都可能在常规任务完成之前改变计划。

00:23:23.976 --> 00:23:55.608
Clinical knowledge, critical thinking and judgment answer different parts of the same task. Knowledge explains the problem; critical thinking tests the information and alternatives; judgment integrates the actual patient, urgency and options. Psychomotor skill makes an authorized procedure reliable, while cognitive and interpersonal skills support decisions, patient understanding and team coordination. A technically smooth action is still wrong if it was not indicated or accepted.
知识、批判性思考和临床判断，处理同一任务的不同方面。知识解释问题，思考检验资料及替代解释，判断则整合患者实际情况、紧急程度和选项。精神运动技能使授权操作可靠，认知与人际技能支持决定、理解和协调。操作即使熟练，没有指征或未获患者接受，仍可能是错误行动。

00:23:55.608 --> 00:24:27.144
Prioritize the threat and allocate personnel, equipment, time and information deliberately. Patient-centered care, evidence, improvement, safety, teamwork and informatics are linked quality themes, not six disconnected definitions. Do not turn a nursing illustration into a new treatment bundle. The book's leg-position, oxygen, fluid or chronic-medicine examples require the actual presentation and current provider guidance, not automatic imitation.
按威胁排序，有意识地分配人员、器械、时间和信息。以人为本、循证改进、安全、团队合作及信息学是相连的主题，而不是六个孤立定义。不能把护理示例变成新的治疗组合。教材中的腿部体位、氧疗、液体或慢性用药示例，都要结合实际表现及现行层级指导，不能自动照做。

00:24:27.144 --> 00:25:00.984
Direct or indirect describes how an action reaches the patient. Independent, dependent or interdependent describes the authority or collaboration behind it. A patient explanation may be direct and within authorized independent practice; obtaining a receiving plan may be indirect and collaborative. Neither classification creates a licence. Similarly, actual, potential and collaborative problems can overlap; a small existing problem does not outrank a credible imminent threat simply because it is actual.
直接或间接，描述行动如何作用于患者；独立、依赖或相互依赖，描述行动背后的权限与协作。向患者解释可以是直接照护，也可属于获授权的独立实践；落实接收计划可以是间接、协作的工作。分类本身不会授予执照。实际、潜在和协作性问题也可能重叠；轻微的现存问题，不会仅因已经发生就优先于可信的迫近威胁。

00:25:00.984 --> 00:25:29.016
Before assigning the second patient, check the five delegation questions: is this the right task and circumstance, is the person competent and authorized, are the instructions clear, and how will supervision and report-back occur? Maintain an overview and an escalation trigger. The textbook's nursing role examples are not universal BC PCP rules, and giving a task does not erase either person's responsibility for their own work.
给同事分派第二名患者的任务前，核对五个方面：任务是否合适、情境是否合适、人员是否具备能力且获授权、指示与沟通是否清楚，以及如何监督并回报。保持整体掌握，明确升级触发点。教材的护理角色示例不是通用的BC PCP规则；分派任务不会消除双方对各自工作的责任。

00:25:29.016 --> 00:25:58.848
Suppose one patient reports less discomfort but becomes harder to engage while breathing grows shallow. Do not declare the goal met from the pain score alone. Assess the actual change and immediate breathing and perfusion needs, then follow the relevant pathway and escalation. Evaluation combines intended benefit, adverse effects and remaining threats. A better monitor number or a completed action does not establish overall recovery.
假设患者不适减轻，却更难交流、呼吸变浅，不能只凭疼痛评分宣布目标达成。评估实际变化和即时呼吸、灌注需要，再按相关流程升级。评价应同时考虑预期获益、不良作用及剩余威胁。数字改善或行动完成，都不能证明患者整体恢复。

00:25:58.848 --> 00:26:30.624
For a met goal, ask what care still has an indication. For a partly met or unmet goal, verify delivery, reconsider the explanation and revise with appropriate consultation. Stopping an unnecessary intervention is different from abandoning the patient. Document the reason, the person's decision, what support continues and who accepts the next plan. Do not independently discontinue prescribed long-term treatment because one teaching example says terminate.
目标达成时，检查哪些措施仍有指征；部分达成或未达成时，核实实施情况，重新考虑解释，并适当咨询、修订。停止不必要的干预，不等于遗弃患者。记录原因、患者决定、继续提供的支持，以及谁接受下一阶段计划。不能因为教学示例提到终止干预，就自行停用长期处方药。

00:26:30.624 --> 00:27:00.048
Use the school's five-minute PCR rehearsal to explain Donabedian. A form and trained crew are structure. An accurate account of both patients, real actions and accepted handover is process. Safety, understanding and continuing care are outcomes to examine. Finishing faster is not proof of improvement if the note omits the quieter patient or invents a normal finding. Measure omissions and errors as well as time.
可用学校的五分钟PCR练习理解Donabedian框架。有记录设备和受训机组属于结构；准确记录两名患者、真实行动及被接受的交接属于过程；安全、理解与照护连续性则是需要核查的结局。若遗漏较安静的患者，或编写正常发现，速度快不能证明质量提高。计时的同时也要检查遗漏和错误。

00:27:00.048 --> 00:27:29.760
Quality assurance asks whether standards and supporting resources are in place; improvement tests ways to make care better. Include patient, team and data perspectives. Patient surveys and nursing-sensitive indicators can reveal gaps, but satisfaction is not a clinical safety certificate and a complication rate alone does not identify its cause. Use clear definitions and comparable populations, not a convenient database name or an isolated score.
质量保证核查标准及支持资源是否到位；质量改进测试如何改善。应纳入患者、团队和数据的视角。体验调查及护理敏感指标可揭示缺口，但满意度不是安全证明，单一并发症率也不能确定原因。需要清楚定义与可比人群，不能只引用数据库名称或孤立分数。

00:27:29.760 --> 00:28:00.408
For each patient, record relevant baseline and changes, actual support and response, the source of information, consultation, specific choices and the accepted next plan. Explain how you know the patient understood, rather than writing understands because a leaflet was supplied. Record the actual intervention, not a request or a prepared dose. Chart promptly when urgent care permits, using the approved process for corrections or late entries.
每名患者都要分别记录相关基线与变化、实际支持及反应、资料来源、咨询、具体选择和已被接受的后续计划。说明如何确认理解，不能因为发过材料就写患者已理解。记录实际干预，不能把请求或备药当成已经执行。紧急照护允许时及时记录；更正和补记须遵循批准流程。

00:28:00.408 --> 00:28:32.280
Objectivity does not mean hiding a clinically important refusal, delay or communication failure. Describe the concern, information exchanged, observed facts and resulting decision without disparaging labels. Immediate danger takes priority over perfect prose; a breathing problem after a medicine cannot wait for a complete paragraph. A truthful record supports continuity and accountability but cannot guarantee a legal outcome or substitute for the care itself.
客观记录并不意味着隐瞒重要拒绝、延误或沟通失败。记录担忧、交换的信息、观察事实及决定，不使用贬损称呼。即时危险优先于完美文字；给药后出现呼吸问题，不能等写完整段记录才处理。真实记录支持连续照护与问责，却不保证法律结果，也不能替代照护本身。

00:28:32.280 --> 00:29:06.624
Source-oriented records group information by form or professional: an admission reference, repeated observations on a flowsheet and a narrative explaining significant events. SOAP instead groups subjective report, objective findings, assessment and plan. SOAPIER adds the actual intervention, evaluation and revision. Separate the interpretation from a confirmed diagnosis, and a plan from what was actually delivered. Use the real required PCR format rather than creating duplicate forms for every acronym.
来源导向记录按表格或专业分类，例如初始资料、记录重复观察的流程表，以及描述重要事件的叙述。SOAP按主观、客观、评估及计划组织，SOAPIER再加入实际干预、评价与修订。区分临床解释与已证实诊断，也区分计划与实际实施。使用真正要求的PCR格式，不必为每个缩写建立重复表格。

00:29:06.624 --> 00:29:37.488
PIE links problem, intervention and evaluation. F-DAR links a focus with data, action and response. Charting by exception requires an approved system and actually assessed norms; it never makes an unexamined system normal. Case-management records track a complex plan across services and time. Whatever the format, another clinician should be able to identify the current concern, what happened, what changed and who owns the unresolved next step.
PIE连接问题、干预和评价；F-DAR连接焦点、资料、行动与反应。例外记录需要获批准的系统，以及真实完成的常规评估，绝不能把未评估写成正常。个案管理跨越服务与时间协调复杂计划。无论格式如何，下一个照护者都应能识别当前担忧、发生的行动、实际变化，以及由谁处理未解决的下一步。

00:29:37.488 --> 00:30:04.656
Return to the feeding-tube patient who is vomiting. First identify immediate airway, breathing and perfusion needs, then examine the symptom and its context. A tube does not explain every episode, and an antiemetic does not confirm tube position or fix an obstruction. Ask what changed from baseline, what preceded the vomiting, and which findings require urgent escalation rather than another routine task.
回到呕吐的喂养管患者。先识别即时气道、呼吸和灌注需要，再了解症状背景。管路问题不能解释每次发作，止吐也不能证明管位正确或梗阻解除。询问相较基线发生了什么变化、呕吐前发生了什么，以及哪些发现需要立即升级，而不是继续完成常规任务。

00:30:04.656 --> 00:30:34.848
The brainstem coordinates inputs from the gut, circulating chemicals, vestibular pathways and higher centers. Receptors explain treatment targets, not the final diagnosis. Antacids neutralize existing acid; they are not all acid-production suppressors and do not treat every cause of nausea. If the patient vomits less but remains distended, poorly perfused or less alert, symptom control has not established recovery.
脑干整合来自消化道、循环中化学物质、前庭及高级中枢的输入。受体说明药物靶点，不是最终诊断。抗酸剂中和已存在的胃酸，并非完全抑制产酸，也不治疗所有恶心。若呕吐减少，但仍有腹胀、灌注不良或意识下降，症状控制仍不等于恢复。

00:30:34.848 --> 00:31:06.720
Map the six families rather than learning one interchangeable antiemetic list. Chlorpromazine and prochlorperazine illustrate dopamine-related phenothiazine effects. Promethazine has stronger antihistamine and anticholinergic characteristics with much weaker dopamine antagonism. Hydroxyzine and meclizine illustrate H one antihistamines; scopolamine illustrates antimuscarinic therapy. A chemical family, receptor effect and clinical indication are three different labels.
用六类机制建立知识图，而不是背诵可互换的止吐药清单。氯丙嗪和丙氯拉嗪体现吩噻嗪类的多巴胺相关作用；异丙嗪更突出抗组胺和抗胆碱作用，多巴胺拮抗较弱。羟嗪和美克洛嗪体现H1作用，东莨菪碱体现抗毒蕈碱作用。化学类别、受体作用和临床指征是不同标签。

00:31:06.720 --> 00:31:36.072
Ondansetron and granisetron target serotonin receptors; aprepitant and rolapitant target the substance P pathway. Many of the reading examples are planned chemotherapy or postoperative prevention, not rescue orders for this device encounter. Dronabinol acts at cannabinoid receptors in a selected chemotherapy setting. These distinctions help you understand a medicine history without making all eleven table prototypes authorized PCP treatments.
昂丹司琼和格拉司琼作用于血清素受体，阿瑞匹坦和罗拉匹坦作用于P物质通路。阅读中的许多示例用于预定化疗或术后预防，不是当前器械患者的急救医嘱。屈大麻酚在特定化疗情境作用于大麻素受体。这些知识有助理解药史，并不会让表中的十一种药都成为PCP获授权的治疗。

00:31:36.072 --> 00:32:04.104
The assigned table contains errors and compressed regimens. Compro is a prochlorperazine product, not a chlorpromazine brand. The dronabinol chemotherapy comparison loses the per-square-meter unit, and the scopolamine line confuses patch content with delivery. A number without the correct drug, formulation, units and indication is not a usable dose. Never repair it by guessing or copying a neighboring row.
指定表格存在错误及被压缩的方案。Compro是丙氯拉嗪产品，不是氯丙嗪商标；屈大麻酚的化疗剂量比较漏掉了每平方米单位；东莨菪碱一行混淆贴剂总含量与实际释放量。药物、剂型、单位或指征不明确时，数字不能用于给药，不能猜补或照抄相邻行。

00:32:04.104 --> 00:32:34.368
Aprepitant illustrates why checking matters more than a quick correction. Weight-based suspension labeling can include adults unable to swallow capsules, so do not declare every adult weight-based entry false. It still needs the right product, population, maximum and later-day regimen. Actual intravenous aprepitant also exists. Likewise, a granisetron chemotherapy schedule is not an automatic repeat-dose rule for every vomiting patient.
阿瑞匹坦说明为何核实比急于纠错更重要。按体重给药的混悬液说明可涵盖不能吞胶囊的成人，因此不能断言所有成人按体重给药都错误；仍须核对产品、人群、上限和后续方案。静脉阿瑞匹坦产品也确实存在。同理，格拉司琼的化疗时序不是所有呕吐患者自动重复给药的规则。

00:32:34.368 --> 00:33:05.232
Suppose the patient is now quieter but harder to engage after a recent medicine. Reassess breathing, consciousness and perfusion instead of recording effective because vomiting stopped. Alcohol, opioids and other depressants can add risk. Watch for hypotension, falls and abnormal movements. An acute dystonic reaction is not simply anxiety, and fever with marked rigidity and altered awareness requires urgent attention rather than a behavioral label.
假设患者近期用药后更安静，却更难交流，应复评呼吸、意识和灌注，不能因为停止呕吐就记录为治疗成功。酒精、阿片类及其他抑制药可增加风险，还要注意低血压、跌倒和异常运动。急性肌张力障碍不能只当作焦虑；发热、强直伴意识改变需要及时处置，不能贴上行为问题标签。

00:33:05.232 --> 00:33:35.040
Anticholinergic effects are particularly relevant to our catheter patient: retention, constipation, blurred vision and confusion may complicate the presentation. A scopolamine patch may be missed in the medication history; handling can transfer medicine to the eye, and reduced sweating can contribute to overheating. A possible medicine effect does not prove causation or exclude another emergency. Keep the actual findings and uncertainty visible.
抗胆碱作用与导尿管患者尤其相关。尿潴留、便秘、视物模糊和意识混乱可能使表现复杂。药史可能漏记东莨菪碱贴剂，接触贴剂后可能把药物带入眼睛，出汗减少也可能促成过热。可能的药物作用不证明因果关系，更不能排除另一急症；保留真实发现与未知。

00:33:35.040 --> 00:34:03.744
Do not flatten all class warnings into one rule. Promethazine injection is contraindicated below age two and still requires caution in older children; it can also cause severe tissue injury. Hydroxyzine injection has its own intramuscular-only restriction and early-pregnancy and prolonged-QT contraindications. These selected label comparisons correct the textbook; they do not authorize you to administer these products or improvise a route.
不能把整类药物的警示压成同一条规则。异丙嗪注射剂禁用于两岁以下儿童，较大儿童仍需谨慎，且可造成严重组织损伤。羟嗪注射剂另有仅限肌注、早孕及QT延长相关禁忌。所选说明用于纠正教材，并不授权使用这些产品或临时改变途径。

00:34:03.744 --> 00:34:38.280
For any authorized medicine, verify the current indication, patient factors, allergies, prior doses, co-medications and exact product instructions. Ondansetron labeling adds QT and serotonergic concerns; nursing antipsychotic mortality warnings have their own context. Access to a tube or vein does not establish compatibility or authority. Use the actual school and service monograph, including the already-taught dimenhydrinate pathway, not the broad chapter as a new formulary.
任何获授权药物都须核实现行指征、患者因素、过敏、既往剂量、合用药及准确产品说明。昂丹司琼说明另有QT与血清素风险，护理阅读中的抗精神病药死亡警示也有各自背景。已有管路或静脉，并不证明兼容或获得权限。使用实际学校与机构专论及已教授的茶苯海明路径，不能把广泛章节当成新的药典。

00:34:38.280 --> 00:35:10.488
Evaluate symptom relief together with consciousness, airway protection, breathing, perfusion and relevant adverse effects. Persistent symptoms require a new look at the cause, not automatic dose stacking. Tailor education and comfort measures: oral fluids or gum are not safe for every swallowing problem, and a fluid-restricted patient does not automatically need extra intake. Explain relevant driving, alcohol and warning-sign advice, then check real understanding.
评价应同时考虑症状缓解、意识与气道保护、呼吸、灌注及相关不良作用。症状持续时重新考虑病因，不自动叠加剂量。教育和舒适措施要个体化：有吞咽困难的人不一定能口服液体或嚼口香糖，限液患者也不能自动增加饮水。解释相关驾驶、酒精及警示事项，再核实真正理解。

00:35:10.488 --> 00:35:38.952
The final assigned page also opens diarrhea assessment. Duration, blood, infection concerns, fluid loss and perfusion matter before deciding whether suppressing stool is appropriate. Apply the same patient-first logic to both device patients and preserve the actual assessment, choices, administered treatment, response and accepted handover in the PCR. A textbook mechanism is useful only when it supports that complete clinical chain.
最后的指定页还开始讨论腹泻评估。在决定是否适合抑制排便前，症状持续时间、便血、感染、体液丢失和灌注都重要。对两名器械患者采用同样的患者优先逻辑，在PCR中保留真实评估与选择、实际治疗及反应，以及已被接受的交接。教材机制只有支持完整临床过程才有用。

00:35:38.952 --> 00:36:06.072
Our catheter patient needs physical help, while the other patient needs a slower explanation. Neither fact tells you they cannot decide. Autonomy, independence and agency are different: a person can need practical assistance and still direct their own care. Ask what each person wants, what support helps and which decision is being made now. Representation starts with their objectives, not with your preferred answer.
导尿管患者需要身体协助，另一名患者需要较慢的解释，都不意味着不能作决定。自主、任务独立和能动感不同；需要实际帮助的人，仍可主导自己的照护。分别询问患者想要什么、何种支持有帮助、当前正在作什么决定。倡导从患者目标开始，而不是从你偏好的答案开始。

00:36:06.072 --> 00:36:36.720
Empowerment develops self-reliance, participation, dignity and belonging. Build on a real strength, explain an option and agree a manageable next step. Practical assistance is not automatically harmful enabling; it may make participation possible. Avoid the rescuer loop in which you take over, the person becomes quieter, and that silence is mistaken for inability. A diagnosis or frequent attendance does not determine worth or comprehension.
赋权支持参与、自立、尊严和归属感。依据真实优势解释选项，商定可行的一步。实际协助不自动等于有害的助长，反而可能使参与成为可能。避免拯救循环：包办后患者沉默，再把沉默解释为无能。诊断或频繁求诊，不能决定一个人的价值或理解能力。

00:36:36.720 --> 00:37:07.632
Use the six trauma-informed practices in the reading: safety, trust, chosen support, partnership, strengths and cultural or gender responsiveness. Introduce the next action before touching a device, explain what is available and invite questions. Include supporters appropriately without automatically disclosing private information or transferring the decision. Transparency matters most when the plan has limits or the patient has had a frightening prior experience.
采用阅读中的六项创伤知情实践，关注安全、信任、患者选择的支持、伙伴关系、优势，以及文化与性别回应。触碰器械前先介绍下一步，解释可行选项并邀请提问。适当邀请支持者，不自动披露私密信息或转移决定权。计划受限或患者有令人恐惧的既往经历时，透明尤其重要。

00:37:07.632 --> 00:37:37.128
Sharing power does not require unsafe treatment or abandoning urgent care. Explain real options and boundaries, assess the specific concern and obtain appropriate help when the lawful route is uncertain. Pain, distress, disability or disagreement alone does not authorize taking over. Preserve participation as far as possible and use the actual consent and service framework, not the textbook's broad nursing examples as an override rule.
共享权力不要求提供不安全治疗，也不意味着放弃紧急照护。解释真实选项和边界，评估具体担忧；法律路径不清时适当求助。疼痛、困扰、障碍或意见分歧，本身都不授权接管决定。尽量保留参与，使用实际的同意与机构框架，而不是让广泛护理示例覆盖本地规则。

00:37:37.128 --> 00:38:01.944
Self-advocacy makes the person's questions and needs heard; it does not require unaided speech. Ask what is unclear, offer a usable explanation and help formulate one question for the next clinician. Model how to clarify an answer, then make room for the person to try. Check what they actually understood instead of treating a leaflet or a family member's agreement as proof.
自我倡导使患者的问题与需要被听见，不要求患者必须在没有帮助时说话。询问哪里不清楚，提供可使用的解释，并帮助形成一个向下一位照护者提出的问题。可以示范如何澄清，再留出患者尝试的空间。核实真正理解，不能把发过材料或家属同意当成证明。

00:38:01.944 --> 00:38:32.184
The six-step judgment model also applies to advocacy. Notice the unanswered concern, analyze its context, identify the priority, generate an appropriate solution, carry it out and evaluate the result. For our quieter patient, that may mean arranging communication support while a colleague maintains the other patient's clinical plan. Verify both the completed explanation and the ongoing assessment; advocacy and safety are not competing tasks.
六步临床判断也适用于倡导：识别未被回应的担忧、分析背景、确定优先事项、形成适当方案、落实及评价。对较安静的患者，可安排沟通支持，同时由同事维持另一名患者的临床计划。核实解释确实完成、评估持续进行；倡导与安全不是相互竞争的任务。

00:38:32.184 --> 00:39:01.032
Use the five advocacy actions to check this encounter. Keep each person informed, mediate the current disagreement respectfully, safeguard against error or privacy loss, show equal dignity and address an actual access barrier. Set a realistic goal and preserve the patient's voice; agreement between professionals is not enough. Escalate a safety concern through the proper route instead of hiding it to avoid tension.
用五项行动核查接触过程：提供信息、尊重患者并处理当前分歧、防范错误与隐私泄露、维护同等尊严，以及处理真实的可及性障碍。设定现实目标，保留患者声音，专业人员之间达成一致仍不够。安全担忧应循正确路径升级，不能为了避免紧张而隐瞒。

00:39:01.032 --> 00:39:31.368
Match the repair to the barrier. Missing equipment needs a resource plan; inaccessible information needs communication support; hierarchy-related fear needs a supported reporting path. In the PCR, preserve choices, supports, real findings and actions, unresolved concerns and accepted handover for each patient. During debrief choose one observable improvement and how to test it next time, not simply that the scene felt calmer or the record was faster.
修复措施要对应障碍。缺少器械需要资源计划，信息难以获取需要沟通支持，畏惧层级需要有支持的报告渠道。PCR应分别保留选择与支持、真实发现和行动、未解决的担忧及已接受的交接。复盘选择一项可观察改进，并说明下次怎样检验，不能只看现场变安静或记录变快。

00:39:31.368 --> 00:39:57.936
A valve lesion is another reason a device patient may deteriorate without the visible tube being the main cause. Begin with the valve as a one-way gate. Stenosis restricts forward passage; regurgitation allows backward leakage. Which chamber and which phase are involved determine the loading pattern. Total blood ejected from a ventricle is not always the amount delivered forward to the organs.
瓣膜病说明，器械患者的恶化未必由最显眼的管路造成。先把瓣膜理解为单向门：狭窄限制前向流动，关闭不全允许反流。受累心腔与心动周期时相决定负荷；心室总射出量不总等于送达器官的有效前向血量。

00:39:57.936 --> 00:40:26.208
Use the normal cycle to orient a murmur. Aortic stenosis obstructs systolic outflow, while mitral regurgitation leaks back during systole. Mitral stenosis obstructs diastolic filling, while aortic regurgitation leaks back during diastole. These mechanisms guide interpretation, not a field anatomy diagnosis. Assess breathlessness, perfusion, rhythm and the change from usual function alongside the sound.
用正常心动周期理解杂音。主动脉瓣狭窄阻碍收缩期流出，二尖瓣反流在收缩期回漏；二尖瓣狭窄阻碍舒张期充盈，主动脉瓣反流在舒张期回漏。机制有助解释，但不是现场解剖诊断。声音要结合气促、灌注、心律及平时功能的变化判断。

00:40:26.208 --> 00:40:56.760
The assigned chapter describes several routes to structural damage. Calcification stiffens tissue; aortic cusps and the mitral annulus have different consequences. A prolapsing mitral leaflet can lose effective closure and cause regurgitation. Rheumatic immune injury can later thicken, fuse and scar the valve and chordae. Do not reverse the prolapse-to-leak explanation or assume rheumatic disease is the only possible cause of mitral stenosis.
点名章节描述多条结构损伤路径。钙化使组织僵硬，主动脉瓣叶与二尖瓣环受累的后果不同；二尖瓣脱垂可使瓣叶不能有效闭合，导致反流；风湿性免疫损伤可使瓣膜与腱索增厚、融合并形成瘢痕。不能把脱垂导致反流的因果关系倒转，也不能把风湿病当成二尖瓣狭窄的唯一原因。

00:40:56.760 --> 00:41:26.376
A chronic lesion may be compensated until another illness increases demand or reduces reserve. Acute severe leakage may produce a rapid change without that adaptation. Ask about known valve disease, repair or replacement, baseline exercise tolerance and the current change when relevant. Then choose the appropriate patient-level pathway. A familiar murmur or a past diagnosis should not distract from a new breathing or perfusion problem.
慢性病可能一直得到代偿，直到另一疾病增加需求或降低储备；急性严重反流则可在尚未来得及适应时迅速恶化。相关时询问已知瓣膜病、修复或置换史、平时活动耐量及当前变化，再选择适合患者的路径。熟悉的杂音或既往诊断，不能分散对新发呼吸与灌注问题的注意。

00:41:26.376 --> 00:41:56.016
Infective vegetations can damage the valve or nearby tissue and send infected or obstructing material elsewhere. Presentation is variable; no fever or no classic peripheral sign cannot exclude the condition. Sterile vegetations are different but not necessarily harmless. Hypercoagulable thrombotic lesions can embolize, and lupus-related lesions involve immune injury. A source photograph is not a diagnosis you can make from one symptom.
感染性赘生物可损伤瓣膜及邻近组织，并向远处播散感染或形成栓塞。表现多变，没有发热或经典外周体征不能排除。无菌性病变机制不同，却未必无害：高凝相关血栓性病变可栓塞，狼疮病变则涉及免疫损伤。不能凭单一症状把来源照片当成诊断。

00:41:56.016 --> 00:42:28.440
Carcinoid mediator injury provides another mechanism, often affecting right-sided valves. For our weekly encounter, use this pathology to widen a thoughtful history, not to invent a rare diagnosis. A new focal deficit, sepsis pattern or acute congestion needs its relevant urgent pathway. Preserve observed findings, uncertainty, authorized support and accepted handover. Neither a loud murmur nor a quiet examination measures the whole risk.
类癌介质损伤是另一机制，常累及右侧瓣膜。本周用病理知识拓展有依据的病史，不虚构罕见诊断。新发局灶缺损、脓毒症模式或急性淤血需要相应的紧急路径。保留观察事实、未知、授权支持与已接受的交接。杂音响亮或检查安静，都不能衡量完整风险。

00:42:28.440 --> 00:42:44.640
The saved school plan names a five-minute PCR completion target for the weekend practice. Treat this as a school exercise standard, not a universal statutory deadline. Use the actual rubric and service PCR system for required fields.
学校保存的计划把五分钟内完成 PCR 作为周末练习目标。应把它视作学校练习标准，而不是普遍的法定时限。必填内容以实际评分表和服务 PCR 系统为准。

00:42:44.640 --> 00:43:04.752
A concise record can still be complete: timeline, patient baseline, device condition, objective findings, actions and response, medication verification, consultation, capacity or consent discussion, and destination handover. Never fabricate a missing detail to meet the timer.
简明记录仍可完整：时间线、患者基线、器械情况、客观发现、行动及反应、药物核对、咨询、能力或同意沟通以及接收交接。绝不能为了赶时间捏造缺失细节。

00:43:04.752 --> 00:43:30.816
The school practises SBAR or MIST. Keep that exercise requirement distinct from current BCEHS A zero three: ATMIST AMBO for transfer of care, and SBAR for consultation. In either setting, communicate the findings, device uncertainty, actions and response, then confirm who accepted the next responsibility. A transmitted report alone is not a completed transfer.
学校练习要求使用SBAR或MIST，应与现行BCEHS A03分清：责任交接采用ATMIST AMBO，咨询采用SBAR。无论哪种情境，都要传递发现、器械相关未知、行动及反应，并确认谁接受了下一项责任。报告发出本身不等于完成责任移交。

00:43:30.816 --> 00:43:43.920
The Week 13 school plan asks the learner to lead all seven debrief questions. Start with the patient’s main problem, then identify the cue that changed your thinking and the competing explanation you considered.
第13周学校计划要求学习者独立主导全部七个复盘问题。先说明患者主要问题，再指出改变你判断的线索及你考虑过的其他解释。

00:43:43.920 --> 00:44:00.576
Next examine the priority, authorized actions and observed response. Finish by naming one specific practice target and how the next run will test it. A debrief should improve the next attempt, not assign blame or merely list the steps.
接着复核优先事项、获准行动和实际反应。最后确定一个具体练习目标，以及下一轮如何检验。复盘应改进下一次尝试，而不是责备个人或只罗列步骤。

00:44:00.576 --> 00:44:15.984
A device can be displaced, blocked or malfunctioning while the patient’s most urgent problem is systemic. Keep the device where it is, avoid unsupported manipulation and use the appropriate pathway to address the patient’s condition.
器械可能移位、堵塞或故障，但患者最紧迫的问题可能是全身性变化。应保持器械现状，避免未经授权的操作，并使用适当流程处理患者状况。

00:44:15.984 --> 00:44:32.016
Full autonomy is visible in the complete loop: assess, prioritize, act within scope, evaluate and communicate. This is the standard you will practise in the device lab, two-patient scenario and timed documentation exercise.
完全自主体现在完整循环中：评估、排序、权限内行动、评价和沟通。接下来的器械实验、双患者情景及计时记录练习都将按这一标准训练。
